<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S9.T7.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">TABLE VII</span>: </span><span id="S9.T7.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">ASR of NeuroStrike under various defenses.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To further assess LSE, we apply NeuroStrike in the white-box setting. The results show that, with safety neuron pruning, the ASR boosts significantly from 16.0% to 86.6% on Gemma-3-1b-it and from 4.8% to 84.7% on QwQ-32B, showing that NeuroStrike can reliably circumvent even internal safety mechanisms when granted full model access.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S10" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">X </span><span id="S10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Ablation and Hyperparameter Study</span></h2>

<section id="S10.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S10.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">X-A</span> </span><span id="S10.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Selection Threshold of Safety Neurons</span></h3>

<div id="S10.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To investigate how the threshold of the <em id="S10.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="S10.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math></em>-score
affects the selection of safety neurons and subsequently impacts attack performance, we perform an ablation study using three representative thresholds: <math id="S10.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=</annotation></semantics></math> 2, 3, and 4.</p>
</div>
